<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107100" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεκ-τίθεμαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bring</i> one's
			property <i>to a place of safety,</i> of persons or things which
			one removes from the dangers of war, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστ᾽ ἂν αὐτοὶ τέκνα τε καὶ τοὺς
					οἰκέτας ὑπεκθέωνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.89
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ χερῶν κλέψασ᾽ Ὀρέστην τῶν ἐμῶν
					ὑπεξέθου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					297
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃν ἔξω δωμάτων ὑπεξέθου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					69
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεκθέμενοι παιδας ἐς Σαλαμῖνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					2.34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τὰ χρήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.1.26
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ὑπεκτεθημένοις</span> (sic) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ βοσκήματα διὰ τὸν πόλεμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BCH</u>
					54.269
				</span></i>
			 (Rhamnus, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>); <i>pueros</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεκθέμενος</span>”
				<i>in Graeciam,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cic.
					<u>Att.</u>
					7.17.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				437.64
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">i B. C.</span>):—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεκτιθέμενοι ἔξω τῆς χώρης οἱ
					παῖδες . . ἥλωσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.65
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>deposit for re-exportation,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ δέ τί κα . . ὑπέχθηται</span>
			(Cret. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέκ-θηται</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5040.21
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεκθέσιμος.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τίθημι,</span>
			<i>expose</i> a new-born child, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Decl.</u>
				34.14
			</span></i>: in 
				Med.
			 simply, <i>bring forth,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεννᾶν καὶ ὑ. τὸν τόκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					4.145a
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
